    <Fragment slot='caption'>
      The stable version of the same page, drawn in the color it deserves: this is the better choice
      among the survivable ones, not a good outcome. The panes' geometry is identical before and
      after the data (the sparse table shows its one row inside its reserved pane, the busy table
      scrolls internally, nothing outside either pane ever moves), but a decision like this
      shouldn't have to be made at all. The real resolution is upstream: layouts, navigation, and
      pages designed to communicate the same information without stacking two unbounded regions on
      one axis in the first place.
