  <h4 id='wizard-shell-sequential'>Sequential flows: one shell, a swappable step</h4>
  <p>
    The correct shape mounts one drawer for the whole flow. The shell (container, header, footer)
    renders once per open; between the static pieces sits a <strong>static content region</strong>
    (<code>flex min-h-0 grow overflow-hidden</code>) that is itself part of the frame. Only the step
    rendered <em>inside</em> that region changes, and the inner frame is what decides how to use the reserved
    space: cap at it and scroll, or take all of it and center.
  </p>

