    <Fragment slot='caption'>
      The sequential anatomy. The outer double-headed arrow: the drawer fills the viewport height and
      disallows overflow, so the frame itself can never grow or scroll. The inner double-headed
      arrow: the static blue content region is what reserves and fills the space between the header
      and the footer, so nothing shifts when the step changes. Either kind of step content then slots
      into that region: the empty or loading state fills the full height and centers its content,
      while the list state caps at the available height and scrolls inside it. The region is fixed;
      only what fills it changes.
