    <pre
      class='code v-good'
      is:raw><span class="filename">AssignLearnersDrawer.tsx - one shell for the whole flow; only the step swaps</span><span class="tok-dir">"use client"</span>;
<span class="tok-com">/* Mounted on open, unmounted on close, dynamically imported by its
   trigger (§8.4). The steps live in their own files. */</span>
<span class="tok-kw">const</span> STEPS = [PickLearners, ReviewConflicts, ConfirmAssignments] <span class="tok-kw">as const</span>;

<span class="tok-kw">export function</span> <span class="tok-fn">AssignLearnersDrawer</span>({ programId, onClose }: <span class="tok-fn">Props</span>) {
  <span class="tok-kw">const</span> [step, setStep] = <span class="tok-fn">useState</span>(<span class="tok-str">0</span>);
  <span class="tok-kw">const</span> Step = STEPS[step];

  <span class="tok-kw">return</span> (
    &lt;<span class="tok-fn">Drawer</span> <span class="tok-prop">onClose</span>={onClose}&gt;
      &lt;div <span class="tok-prop">className</span>=<span class="tok-str">"flex max-h-full grow flex-col overflow-hidden"</span>&gt;
        <span class="tok-com">{/* Static: rendered once per open; never changes per step. */}</span>
        &lt;<span class="tok-fn">DrawerHeader</span> <span class="tok-prop">title</span>=<span class="tok-str">"Assign learners"</span> <span class="tok-prop">onClose</span>={onClose} /&gt;

        <span class="tok-com">{/* Static container: reserves everything between the header and
            the footer and never changes. Only the step INSIDE it swaps;
            the step's inner frame decides how to use the space. */}</span>
        &lt;div <span class="tok-prop">className</span>=<span class="tok-str">"flex min-h-0 grow flex-col overflow-hidden"</span>&gt;
          &lt;<span class="tok-fn">Step</span> <span class="tok-prop">programId</span>={programId} /&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;

        <span class="tok-com">{/* Static: the buttons never move under the user's cursor. */}</span>
        &lt;<span class="tok-fn">DrawerFooter</span>&gt;
          &lt;<span class="tok-fn">Button</span> <span class="tok-prop">onClick</span>={() =&gt; <span class="tok-fn">setStep</span>((s) =&gt; s - <span class="tok-str">1</span>)} <span class="tok-prop">disabled</span>={step === <span class="tok-str">0</span>}&gt;
            Previous
          &lt;/<span class="tok-fn">Button</span>&gt;
          &lt;<span class="tok-fn">Button</span> <span class="tok-prop">onClick</span>={() =&gt; <span class="tok-fn">setStep</span>((s) =&gt; s + <span class="tok-str">1</span>)}&gt;
            {step === STEPS.length - <span class="tok-str">1</span> ? <span class="tok-str">"Finish"</span> : <span class="tok-str">"Next"</span>}
          &lt;/<span class="tok-fn">Button</span>&gt;
        &lt;/<span class="tok-fn">DrawerFooter</span>&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/<span class="tok-fn">Drawer</span>&gt;
  );
}</pre>
    <CodeCaption>
      Three steps, one drawer. The shell (container, header, footer) renders when the drawer opens
      and is never rebuilt; advancing the wizard changes <code>STEPS[step]</code> and nothing else. The
      wrong version mounts a different drawer per step, and the user watches the frame they were standing
      in tear down and reassemble on every click.
    </CodeCaption>
  </Snippet>

  <Snippet>
    <pre
      class='code v-good'
      is:raw><span class="filename">PickLearners.tsx - dynamic content slotting into the static frame</span><span class="tok-dir">"use client"</span>;
<span class="tok-kw">export function</span> <span class="tok-fn">PickLearners</span>({ programId }: { programId: <span class="tok-kw">string</span> }) {
  <span class="tok-kw">const</span> { data: learners } = <span class="tok-fn">useLearners</span>(programId);

  <span class="tok-com">/* Unknown or empty: the static container already reserved the space.
     Take all of it (h-full + min-h-full) and center the children within
     it: the centering is free because the height is real and fixed. */</span>
  <span class="tok-kw">if</span> (!learners || learners.length === <span class="tok-str">0</span>) {
    <span class="tok-kw">return</span> (
      &lt;div <span class="tok-prop">className</span>=<span class="tok-str">"flex h-full min-h-full items-center justify-center"</span>&gt;
        {learners ? <span class="tok-str">"No learners to assign."</span> : &lt;<span class="tok-fn">Spinner</span> /&gt;}
      &lt;/div&gt;
    );
  }

  <span class="tok-com">/* List content: caps at the reserved height and scrolls inside it.
     No grow, no min-h-0: the container already owns the geometry. */</span>
  <span class="tok-kw">return</span> (
    &lt;ul <span class="tok-prop">className</span>=<span class="tok-str">"max-h-full overflow-y-auto"</span>&gt;
      {learners.map((l) =&gt; (
        &lt;<span class="tok-fn">LearnerRow</span> <span class="tok-prop">key</span>={l.id} <span class="tok-prop">learner</span>={l} /&gt;
      ))}
    &lt;/ul&gt;
  );
}</pre>
    <CodeCaption>
      Both fill modes of the inner frame, against the same reserved space. A spinner or empty
      message takes the full height (<code>h-full</code>) and centers within it; a list caps at that
      height (<code>max-h-full</code>) and scrolls inside it with <code>overflow-y-auto</code>; and
      in neither case does the drawer's frame move a pixel. The panel showing its own loading
      indicator is the legitimate case (<a href='15-dedupe-caching.html#when-client'>§15.7</a>): the
      drawer is the container, and its content was never knowable before the click.
    </CodeCaption>
  </Snippet>

